UPDATE companies SET description='GAMA Electronics Inc. operates from Woodstock, Illinois, about fifty miles northwest of Chicago. The company was founded in 1990 by John and Irene Golbeck, who continue to manage the business alongside their son Tom.

The company designs and manufactures electronic and electromechanical controls, including custom electronic assemblies, switches, control panels, and wireless remote controls. Its Woodstock facility handles both through-hole and surface-mount PCB assembly, mechanical assembly, wire harnessing, and packaging. Production scales from low-volume runs to high-volume sustained production, supported by factory automation and manual assembly. The engineering team provides complete circuit and PCB design, software development, mechanical design (sheet metal, injection-molded plastic, graphical overlays), and in-house prototyping.

GAMA serves transportation, industrial equipment, medical, agriculture, and marine markets. In transportation, it supplies PCB assemblies, control panels, switches, and harnesses, including patented battery disconnect switches and high-volume cruise control switch assemblies for a major U.S. automotive manufacturer. Industrial customers use motor controls, access controls, remote controls, HVAC controls, gym equipment controls, winch and hoist controls, and lighting controls. Medical work includes heat sealer products (via the Steri Sealer line) and custom assemblies for X-ray machinery, pharmaceutical dispensing equipment, and patient assist devices. Agricultural applications feature remote control systems, motor control assemblies, and custom control panels.

The company emphasizes its U.S.-based production facility combined with global alliances to offer competitive pricing and timely delivery. Its ISO 9001 certification underpins quality assurance, and the firm highlights a family-oriented work culture as a driver of customer satisfaction.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electronic assembly", "Control systems", "Motor controls", "Electronic design", "Switches and relays", "Development and manufacturing", "PCB assembly (through-hole)", "PCB assembly (surface mount)", "Mechanical assembly", "Wire harnessing", "Packaging", "Circuit design", "PCB design", "Software design", "Mechanical design (sheet metal, injection molded plastic, graphical overlay)", "In-house prototyping", "Custom electronic controls", "Custom control panels", "Wireless remote controls", "Battery disconnect switches", "Cruise control switch assembly", "Heat sealer manufacturing", "Remote control systems for commercial overhead doors", "Boat lift remote control systems"], "industries": ["Transportation", "Industrial Equipment", "Medical", "Agriculture", "Marine"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low volume to high volume sustained production runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Woodstock, Illinois -> db", "Founded 1990 by John & Irene Golbeck -> /about-us", "Family-owned, managed with son Tom -> /about-us", "Full service electronic products manufacturer -> /", "Capabilities: electronic assemblies, control systems, motor controls, electronic design, switches, relays, development, manufacturing -> /", "PCB assembly (thru-hole and surface mount), mechanical assembly, wire harnessing, packaging -> /capabilities", "Production rates: low volume to high volume sustained -> /capabilities", "Factory automation and manual assembly -> /capabilities", "Design services: circuit/PCB design, software design, mechanical design (sheet metal, injection molded plastic, graphical overlay), in-house prototyping -> /capabilities", "Industries: Transportation, Industrial Equipment, Medical, Agriculture, Marine -> /about-us, /", "Transportation examples: PCB assemblies, control panels, switches, harnesses, battery disconnect switches, cruise control switch assembly for major US automotive manufacturer -> /", "Industrial examples: motor controls, access controls, remote controls, HVAC controls, gym equipment controls, winch/lift/hoist controls, lighting controls -> /", "Medical examples: heat sealer products (Steri Sealer), custom assemblies for X-ray, pharmaceutical dispensing, patient assist devices -> /", "Agriculture examples: remote control systems, motor control assemblies, custom control panels -> /", "ISO 9001 certification -> /about-us", "U.S. production facility with global alliances -> /about-us, /capabilities", "Family-oriented work culture -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a full service electronic products manufacturer.", "founded_year": "1990", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='gama-electronics-plant-2' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='GAO RFID Inc., a member of the GAO Group, is headquartered in Toronto, Ontario, Canada, with a U.S. office in Manhattan, New York. The company is incorporated in both Canada and the United States and has over 30 years of experience delivering RFID and Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) solutions.

The company designs and manufactures a broad range of RFID and BLE hardware, including readers, tags, antennas, printers, and gateways covering frequencies from low frequency (125/134 kHz) and high frequency (13.56 MHz) to UHF (865–928 MHz) and active 2.5 GHz bands. Its middleware platform serves as a modular software engine for customizable RFID systems, and the firm offers integration, consulting, site surveys, and software customization. GAO RFID reports more than 11,000 system deployments across 70 countries.

Customers range from small and mid-sized enterprises to Fortune 500 companies, educational institutions, and government agencies. The company serves industries such as agriculture, oil and gas, manufacturing, supply chain and logistics, transportation, railway, automotive, education, healthcare, retail, cold chain, livestock management, and data centers.

GAO RFID emphasizes overnight delivery within the continental U.S. and Canada from local warehouses, on-site expert support, and hardware that is designed, manufactured, and tested in-house. Its team includes CompTIA RFID+ certified professionals, and its middleware architecture enables rapid customization for specific industry needs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["RFID reader design and manufacturing", "RFID tag design and manufacturing", "BLE gateway and beacon design and manufacturing", "RFID antenna and peripheral manufacturing", "RFID middleware development", "RFID system integration", "RFID consulting", "RFID site survey", "Software customization", "Technical support and warranty services", "Overnight delivery (logistics)"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Oil & Gas", "Manufacturing", "Supply Chain", "Logistics", "Transportation", "Railway", "Automotive", "Education", "Healthcare", "Retail", "Government", "Data Center", "Cold Chain", "Livestock"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Overnight delivery within continental U.S. and Canada for stocked hardware", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Overnight delivery within continental U.S. and Canada from local warehouse", "On-site expert support available", "Hardware designed, manufactured, and tested in-house", "Over 30 years of experience with 11,000+ deployments in 70+ countries", "CompTIA RFID+ certified engineering and sales staff"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Toronto, Canada; U.S. office in Manhattan, New York -> /about", "Incorporated in Canada and USA -> /about", "Over 30 years of experience -> /about, /", "11,000+ RFID/BLE systems deployed in 70+ countries -> /", "Designs and manufactures RFID/BLE hardware (readers, tags, antennas, printers, gateways) -> /, /about", "Middleware platform for customizable software -> /, /about", "Services: integration, consulting, site surveys, software customization -> /services, /about", "Customers: SMEs to Fortune 500, educational, government agencies -> /about", "Industries served: agriculture, oil & gas, manufacturing, supply chain, logistics, transportation, railway, automotive, education, healthcare, retail, cold chain, livestock, data centers -> /, /about", "Overnight delivery within continental US & Canada from local warehouse -> /about, /services", "On-site expert support -> /about, /services", "Hardware designed, manufactured, tested in-house -> /about, /services", "CompTIA RFID+ certified professionals -> /about", "Member of GAO Group -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "GAO RFID Inc. designs and manufactures advanced RFID products", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='gao-rfid' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='GEM Equipment of Oregon, Inc. was founded in 1968 in Woodburn, Oregon, by co-founder Ed McKenney. Starting with limited resources but a clear vision to deliver equipment that meets real-world processing needs through close collaboration with customers, the company began as a custom food processing equipment specialist.

The company designs, builds, and installs advanced frying systems, including fryers, blanchers, and batter application systems, for food manufacturers worldwide. As part of FPS Food Process Solutions—a global leader in turnkey food processing—GEM leverages computational fluid dynamics (CFD) modelling, stainless steel fabrication, and a global service network with remote diagnostics to deliver integrated fried food production lines.

GEM serves the food processing industry, with a focus on fried food production such as French fries, potato chips, vegetables, seafood, and malting. Its equipment has been supplied to major processors including General Foods, Ore-Ida, Simplot, McCain Foods, and Lamb Weston.

