UPDATE companies SET description='Global Bridge Pharmaceutical is a pharmacist-led pharmaceutical distribution and consulting company headquartered in Charlotte, North Carolina. The company was founded by a team of professionals with a combined 55 years of experience in healthcare and drug regulation.

The firm provides a range of pharmaceutical supply chain services including prescription drug procurement, pharmacovigilance and drug safety support, managed access and patient support programs, global access and export solutions, strategic sourcing, hospital supply chain support, and emergency procurement for drug shortages. It also offers drug information consulting, after-sales training, and collaboration on humanitarian public health projects. Global Bridge maintains offices in Charlotte, North Carolina; Ferrara, Italy; and Douala, Cameroon.

Its customer base spans hospitals and health systems, clinics and pharmacies, government agencies and non-governmental organizations, pharmaceutical manufacturers, and public health organizations. The company works with healthcare providers, specialty practices, and charitable programs to address medication shortages, sourcing challenges, and continuity-of-care needs both domestically and internationally.

Global Bridge differentiates itself through its pharmacist-led leadership, an agile network of licensed suppliers, and a social impact initiative called RxSecondHome™ that redirects excess and short-dated medicines to underserved patients. The company emphasizes compliant sourcing under FDA and DSCSA regulations and aims to reduce pharmaceutical waste while expanding access to affordable therapies.', certifications=ARRAY['FDA registered','DSCSA compliant','MBE certified','SAM registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Rx Procurement", "Pharmacovigilance & Drug Safety Services", "Managed Access & Patient Support Programs", "Global Access & Export Solutions", "Strategic Pharmaceutical Sourcing", "Hospital Supply Chain Support", "Drug Shortage & Emergency Procurement", "Excess Pharmaceutical Repurposing", "Drug Information & Consulting Services", "After-Sales Training Programs", "Humanitarian & Public Health Project Collaboration"], "industries": ["Hospitals & Health Systems", "Clinics & Pharmacies", "Government Agencies", "Non-Governmental Organizations", "Pharmaceutical Manufacturers", "Public Health Organizations", "Specialty Practices", "Healthcare Providers"], "materials": ["Pharmaceuticals", "Prescription medicines"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Pharmacist-led team with combined 55 years of healthcare and regulatory experience", "FDA-registered and DSCSA-compliant operations", "Agile network of licensed suppliers and industry partners", "Social impact initiative RxSecondHome\u2122 redistributes excess and short-dated medicines"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Charlotte, North Carolina -> /", "Pharmacist-led pharmaceutical distribution and consulting company -> /", "Founded by professionals with combined 55 years experience -> /about-us", "Certified Minority Business Entity (MBE), HUB Certified, SAM registered -> /about-us", "FDA registered and DSCSA compliant -> /about-us", "CAGE code 8F8E7 -> /about-u