UPDATE companies SET description='GlobalFoundries was founded in 2009 as a joint venture between Mubadala Investment Company and Advanced Micro Devices (AMD) to address growing global demand for advanced semiconductors. The company established its global headquarters and flagship fabrication facility in Malta, New York, marking the first advanced foundry built in the United States in decades.

The company operates as a pure-play semiconductor foundry, offering a differentiated portfolio of process technologies including CMOS, FinFET, FDX™ FD-SOI, RF-SOI, SiGe, BCD, power GaN, and silicon photonics. Its manufacturing footprint spans five sites: Malta (NY), Burlington (VT), Dresden (Germany), Singapore, and Guangzhou (China). The Malta campus serves as a highly automated 300mm fab, while Burlington specializes in RF and GaN technologies. GlobalFoundries provides end-to-end services from wafer fabrication and bump (200mm/300mm) through advanced packaging (2.5D/3D, wafer-to-wafer, die-to-wafer), assembly, and test, supported by a vetted network of OSAT partners. Headcount ranges from 5,000 to 9,999 employees.

GlobalFoundries serves fabless semiconductor companies, integrated device manufacturers, and system houses across aerospace & defense, automotive, data center & communications infrastructure, home & industrial IoT, and smart mobile devices. Notable collaborations include a multi-year agreement with Marvell for high-performance SiGe optical connectivity, a partnership with TSMC to establish a U.S.-based source of silicon interposers for CoWoS® advanced packaging, and the acquisition of MIPS to strengthen processor IP capabilities.

The company positions itself as a differentiated technology partner that combines R&D, IP, design, custom silicon, and advanced manufacturing across a flexible global footprint. Its stated mission is to deliver "trusted, essential chips through deep customer co-innovation and partnerships," emphasizing supply chain resilience and manufacturing optionality for security-critical and high-growth markets.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CMOS fabrication", "FinFET fabrication", "FDX\u2122 FD-SOI", "RF-SOI", "SiGe BiCMOS", "BCD (Bipolar-CMOS-DMOS)", "Power GaN", "Silicon photonics", "Quantum technology processing", "Advanced packaging (2.5D/3D, wafer-to-wafer, die-to-wafer)", "Wafer bumping (SnAg, copper pillar, WLCSP) for 200mm and 300mm", "Wafer sort with Known Good Die methodology", "Backside grind, dicing, marking, binning", "Module assembly and packaging", "RF testing (high/low temperature, analog/digital TxRx, mmWave)", "Memory testing (eNVM)", "High-speed interface test", "High-voltage/high-current testing", "ATE test program development", "Package engineering (electrical, thermal, mechanical analysis)", "Reliability stress services (JEDEC, Mil-std, AEC)", "Engineering and debugging services", "Design services for manufacturability", "MIPS processor IP integration"], "industries": ["Aerospace & defense", "Automotive", "Data center & communications infrastructure", "Home & industrial IoT", "Smart mobile devices", "Microelectronics", "Wireless", "IoT"], "materials": ["Silicon", "Silicon Germanium (SiGe)", "Gallium Nitride (GaN)", "Silicon-on-Insulator (SOI)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 2009 as joint venture between Mubadala and AMD -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Malta, New York -> db, /", "Employee count 5000-9999 -> db", "Operates fabs in Malta, Burlington, Dresden, Singapore, Guangzhou -> /", "Offers CMOS, FinFET, FD-SOI, RF-SOI, SiGe, BCD, Power GaN, sili