UPDATE companies SET description='Gold Path Solar is headquartered in Greenville, South Carolina, and serves property owners across Ohio, Kentucky, and South Carolina. The company was formed after its leadership team accumulated more than 20 years of experience in the solar industry, though a specific founding year is not disclosed. It is structured as an employee-owned business, a model the founders chose to align long-term customer outcomes with the financial interests of the people doing the work.

The company designs and installs residential and commercial photovoltaic systems and integrates battery storage. Its in-house teams handle system engineering, permitting, utility interconnection, and physical installation, using Enphase microinverters for panel-level production. The average residential installation is completed in one day; larger or more complex projects may require additional time. No facility size, headcount, or annual volume figures are published.

Gold Path Solar works with homeowners, businesses, farms, nonprofits, and commercial property owners. Each project begins with a no-obligation consultation and a dedicated Solar Advocate who remains the single point of contact through design, permitting, installation, and activation. The company cites its employee-owned structure and the dedicated-advocate model as direct responses to common industry complaints about high-pressure sales, poor communication, and subcontracted labor.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar system design and installation", "Commercial solar system design and installation", "Battery storage system integration", "Permitting and utility interconnection management", "Site survey and engineering plan preparation", "System monitoring setup and post-installation support"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Agricultural", "Nonprofit", "Commercial property"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Enphase microinverters"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Average residential installation completed in one day", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Employee-owned structure aligns installer incentives with customer outcomes", "Dedicated Solar Advocate serves as single point of contact from consultation through activation", "In-house installation teams; no third-party subcontractors", "Average residential installation completed in one day", "Full permitting and utility interconnection managed internally"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Greenville, SC -> db", "Serves Ohio, Kentucky, South Carolina -> /", "Employee-owned structure stated multiple times -> /, /about-us", "Founded after 20+ years industry experience (no explicit year) -> /, /about-us", "In-house installation teams, no third-party labor -> /, /about-us", "Uses Enphase microinverters -> / (products list)", "5-step process: consultation, site survey, permits, installation, activation -> /, /about-us", "Dedicated Solar Advocate single point of contact ->