UPDATE companies SET description='Grace Technologies is headquartered in Davenport, Iowa. The company traces its roots to 1993 when founder Phil Allen, while working on a friction welder retrofit at John Deere, identified a hazardous electrical access issue and launched Grace Engineering to develop the GracePort panel interface connector. The business evolved into Grace Engineered Products and was renamed Grace Technologies in 2020 to reflect its expanded portfolio. Leadership remains in the family: Phil Allen serves as Chairman of the Board, and his son Drew Allen is President and CEO.

Grace manufactures three core product lines: GracePort panel interface connectors that provide thru-door programming access to PLCs and control panels; GracePESDs, permanent electrical safety devices that combine presence-of-voltage LED indication with absence-of-voltage test points for lockout/tagout verification; and the GraceSense predictive maintenance system, IIoT smart sensors that continuously monitor vibration and temperature on switchgears, transformers, and rotating equipment. The company maintains roughly 16,000 active SKUs and ships orders worldwide within two to three business days through a distribution network spanning more than 60 countries.

The devices are designed for low- to medium-voltage applications and are used to make maintenance safer, smarter, and more productive.

Grace emphasizes four differentiators: thought leadership in electrical safety, mass customization enabled by its large SKU count, fast global delivery, and a founding principle of being easy to do business with. Its stated mission is to pursue practical ways of keeping live voltage away from workers before, during, and after maintenance tasks, while empowering maintenance programs with IIoT sensor data.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical safety device manufacturing", "Panel interface connector design and manufacturing", "Permanent electrical safety device (PESD) manufacturing", "Predictive maintenance IIoT sensor manufacturing", "Vibration monitoring", "Temperature monitoring", "Mass customization", "Global distribution and logistics", "Lockout/tagout verification solutions"], "industries": ["Incident Energy Exposure"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "2-3 business days for worldwide shipping", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Thought leadership in electrical safety", "Mass customization with ~16,000 SKUs", "Worldwide shipping in 2-3 business days", "Easy to do business with as a founding principle"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1993 by Phil Allen -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Davenport, Iowa -> db", "Renamed to Grace Technologies in 2020 -> /about-us", "Products: GracePort, GracePESDs, GraceSense -> /about-us and /", "16,000 SKUs -> /about-us", "Ships worldwide in 2-3 business days -> /about-us", "Operates in 60+ countries -> /about-us", "Family leadership: Phil Allen (Chairman), Drew Allen (President & CEO) -> /about-us", "Mission: keep live voltage away from workers -> /about-us", "Differentiators: thought leadership, mass customization, fast delivery, easy to do business with -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, Grace manufacturers and delivers electrical safety innovations and predictive maintenance solutions through a global distribution network", "founded_year": "1993", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='grace-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Grado Creations operates from Albuquerque, New Mexico. The company traces its roots to the handcrafted heritage of custom woodworking led by master craftsman Jose Grado, and has since evolved into a made-to-order home textiles brand.

The workshop produces quilted bedding sets, reversible sofa slipcovers, area rugs, and seasonal home accents. Each piece is made to order using direct-to-textile dye printing, precision stitching, and multi-layer quilting with water-resistant barriers and hypoallergenic fills. Production is scaled to individual orders rather than warehouse stock.

The brand serves residential customers across the United States seeking rustic, Southwestern-inspired home decor that withstands daily life with pets and children. Retail partners are also mentioned in earlier descriptions, though the current focus appears direct-to-consumer.

