UPDATE companies SET description='Grand Central Wiring was founded in 2006 by Jason Gillespie in Greenville, South Carolina. The company began as an audio/video design and installation firm, later expanding into security, automation, and structured wiring services for both residential and commercial clients.

Today the business provides a full range of technology integration services, including TV mounting, custom home theater design, universal remote programming, distributed audio, network and structured wiring, video surveillance, smart home automation, lighting control, and electrical wiring. It also offers construction-related services such as sheetrock repair, painting, framing, and masonry to support design-build cinema projects.

Clients include homeowners, business owners, and home builders. Grand Central Wiring wires for all major local TV and internet providers—Charter, AT&T, DirecTV, and Dish—and collaborates with licensed builder Phil Gillespie on design-build cinema installations. The company serves both residential and commercial spaces, from private home theaters to office lobby displays.

